{"id": "EUVD-2026-101865", "enisaUuid": "eb4febe0-6543-3756-a97d-756c87e4dfd8", "description": "When fdescfs(4) was mounted in a jail with the \"nodup\" option, opening /dev/fd/N returned a descriptor that did not inherit FD_RESOLVE_BENEATH or the Capsicum capability rights of descriptor N.\n\nA process in a jail that has received a directory file descriptor from another jail can use these techniques to escape the jail's filesystem root restriction.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T06:46:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:53:31", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://security.freebsd.org/advisories/FreeBSD-SA-26:66.jail.asc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-101304"], "assigner": "freebsd", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0059ac69-268b-395b-9b8c-afecec2e8bf7", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "14.4-RELEASE <p10"}, {"id": "5f546889-9726-31c6-80bc-38360bb1c522", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "14.5-RELEASE <p1"}, {"id": "b3e71b0b-09dd-383b-bd60-8c03e9c878f0", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "15.0-RELEASE <p14"}, {"id": "b582765d-6053-3a34-9090-57737ecd07e5", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "15.1-RELEASE <p4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "659d0ab7-bab8-308c-be5c-9f34310be0df", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}], "isExploited": false}